The above data is available as a [text file](../../datasets/COMPARE-7_1_6.DAT).

The computations are as follows:


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
y <- outlier_data$Value
n <- length(y)

med <- median(y)
q1 <- quantile(y, 0.25, type = 6, names = FALSE)
q3 <- quantile(y, 0.75, type = 6, names = FALSE)
iq <- q3 - q1

tibble(
  Statistic = c("Median", "Lower quartile", "Upper quartile", "Interquartile range", "Lower inner fence", "Upper inner fence", "Lower outer fence", "Upper outer fence"),
  Value = c(med, q1, q3, iq, q1 - 1.5 * iq, q3 + 1.5 * iq, q1 - 3 * iq, q3 + 3 * iq)
) |>
  knitr::kable(digits = 2, align = "lr")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}


|Statistic           |   Value|
|:-------------------|-------:|
|Median              |  559.50|
|Lower quartile      |  429.75|
|Upper quartile      |  742.25|
|Interquartile range |  312.50|
|Lower inner fence   |  -39.00|
|Upper inner fence   | 1211.00|
|Lower outer fence   | -507.75|
|Upper outer fence   | 1679.75|


:::
:::


- Median = $(N+1)/2$ largest data point = the average of the 45th and 46th ordered points = (559 + 560)/2 = 559.5
- [Lower quartile](#sec-prc-262) = $.25(N+1)$th ordered point = 22.75th ordered point = 411 + .75(436-411) = 429.75
- [Upper quartile](#sec-prc-262) = $.75(N+1)$th ordered point = 68.25th ordered point = 739 + .25(752-739) = 742.25
- Interquartile range = 742.25 - 429.75 = 312.5
- Lower inner fence = 429.75 - 1.5 (312.5) = -39.0
- Upper inner fence = 742.25 + 1.5 (312.5) = 1211.0
- Lower outer fence = 429.75 - 3.0 (312.5) = -507.75
- Upper outer fence = 742.25 + 3.0 (312.5) = 1679.75

From an examination of the fence points and the data, one point (1441) exceeds the upper inner fence and stands out as a mild outlier; there are no extreme outliers.

[**Histogram with box plot**]{#sec-prc-16-histogram}

A histogram with an overlaid box plot are shown below.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
library(patchwork)

x_breaks <- seq(0, 1500, by = 500)
x_limits <- c(0, 1650)

p_box <- ggplot(outlier_data, aes(x = Value, y = 1)) +
  geom_boxplot() +
  labs(x = NULL, y = NULL) +
  scale_x_continuous(breaks = x_breaks, limits = x_limits) +
  scale_y_continuous(breaks = NULL) +
  theme_light() +
  theme(axis.text.x = element_blank())

p_hist <- ggplot(outlier_data, aes(Value)) +
  geom_histogram(binwidth = 200, boundary = 0, fill = "lightblue", color = "black") +
  labs(x = "Data Values", y = "Frequency") +
  scale_x_continuous(breaks = x_breaks, limits = x_limits) +
  theme_light()

p_box / p_hist + plot_layout(heights = c(1, 4))
```

